<%#
  One answered step, collapsed.

  Reads the entry and only the entry. Steps get edited and deleted after runs,
  so a card built from the live Step record would replay a call with text nobody
  ever saw, or fail on a uuid that no longer resolves.

  A card, not a line of text. It was a single line first, on the theory that a
  scanning surface pays for height in how much of the call stays visible — but
  that was protecting a behaviour nobody had watched, and the numbers did not
  support it: 69px against 38px, over a median completed run of 12 steps, is
  about half a screen. What the card buys is weight. An answered step is a
  decision somebody made on a live call, and scrolling back to re-read one is a
  real thing agents do; `title → answer` on one line is thin for that.

  locals: entry
%>
<% summary = runner_row_summary(entry) %>
<li class="runner-thread__card"
    style="--thread-depth: <%= runner_thread_indent(entry) %>; --step-hue: var(<%= runner_entry_hue(entry) %>);">
  <span class="runner-thread__check" aria-hidden="true">
    <%= icon "check", class: "icon icon--xs" %>
  </span>
  <div class="runner-thread__card-body">
    <span class="sr-only">Completed.</span>
    <span class="runner-thread__kind"><%= runner_entry_kind(entry) %></span>
    <span class="runner-thread__card-title"><%= entry["step_title"] %></span>
    <% if summary.present? %>
      <span class="runner-thread__card-answer"><%= summary %></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</li>
